Subject: Observed Field Attention Fault Assurance Evidence

Description: Preserved verifier-audit observation distinguishing replayed provider evidence from structurally valid runtime-fault declarations. This is observed engineering evidence, not user dictation and not implementation authority by itself.

@ [source_snapshot_uuid] 7a9755a3-1219-4d32-bf11-4acf9694dcf4
@ [conversation_uuid] 019f94c8-da23-7131-aef2-6ac02612d155
@ [observed_on] 2026-08-18

& [ExistingAuthority] requires inspectable replay without converting model or runtime output into truth
  + exact stored provider requests and responses already reconstruct probes candidates delineation latch and response-backed faults
  + runtime failures must remain preservable as typed evidence rather than being erased

& [ObservedGap] is assurance-class collapse
  + ReportVerification valid currently covers both fully recomputed stored-provider lineage and a runtime-fault shape with no retained failed response
  + a network timeout connection failure or local I/O fault can have a canonical event path while its external cause cannot be replayed from report bytes
  + callers cannot distinguish those evidence strengths from the machine result alone

& [Risk] is representational overstatement
  + structural validity may be read as proof that an unretained external failure happened exactly as described
  + rejecting all unbacked runtime faults would erase operational evidence and make failure preservation less honest

& [RequiredDisposition] is a closed assurance vocabulary
  + deterministic construction identifies the exact host fixture
  + stored provider replay identifies completed rejected and control reports reconstructed from retained exchanges
  + response-backed fault replay identifies a fault recomputed from one retained failed provider response
  + structural runtime fault only identifies a canonical fault trajectory whose external cause is declared but not replayable
  + expose the assurance class in every verification result and test each class
  - never: convert any assurance class into truth safety authorization effect permission or proof of unobserved external state
